# The wizard's fire on the worn suit, and the suit's page either side.
# Included by quality-self-immune-plain.keys and quality-self-immune-quality.keys,
# AFTER each of those has or has not put the quality on the suit.
# Read by tools/check_quality_self_immune.sh (bd inc-to9x, inc-aoi4i).
#
# THE BURN is the wizard command "Burn Worn Armour" (src/Debug.cpp, inc-aoi4i):
# a fixed 10 points of fire to the suit in the armour slot, sent with no actor
# and no random number. quality-self-immune-setup.keys says why the burn
# is a wizard command. It replaces the three hell hounds and the hundred turns of their
# breath, which depended on monster AI and on coin tosses in Magic::Blast.
#
# THE ORACLE is the suit's own page, read before and after. Its hit points are
# the behavioural half; its hardness table, which ItemHardnessDesc builds by
# calling Item::Hardness once per damage type, is the direct half. The game's
# combat-numbers line (src/Item.cpp:1511-1531) prints "vs. 0 (leather)" or
# "vs. Immune (leather)" as it happens, but only the LAST such line survives to
# a screen dump, so no assertion rests on catching one.

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>j)Armour" j
@until "base value of" x
@dump:burn-before
@until "Things in View" ESC

# Nothing hostile may interrupt the scroll reading that follows. Wizard option
# 11 counted from the top of src/Debug.cpp:544 kills every monster on the level
# and costs no game time.
w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
@while "Die?" n
@while "more --" SPACE
@until "Things in View" ESC

w
@choose "Burn Worn Armour"
@while "more --" SPACE
@until "Things in View" ESC

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>j)Armour" j
@until "base value of" x
@dump:burn-after
@until "Things in View" ESC
